# Rule - Incremental Delivery

Finish one backlog item before you start the next.

Feature versus task breakdown is in `{client_root}/templates/framework.sdd.works/sdd-scrum-practices.md`, section **5. Feature break down**. `sdd-refine-backlog` and `sdd-plan-sprint` follow that section. This rule does not repeat it.

## Current item

The current item is the one named in `status.md`. Open `status.md` through `{workspace}/artifacts-map.json`.

The item is finished on the board only when [`sdd-dod.mdc`](./sdd-dod.mdc) passes, including **close confirm**. Meeting acceptance criteria or shipping files does not set the row to **Done** by itself. The item may be a product backlog item (PBI) or a sprint backlog item (SBI).

## Behavior

- Do not start another item while the current one is not Done.
- After the last edit for the current SBI, stop and invoke **close confirm** from `sdd-dod.mdc`. Do not write **Done** on `sprint-backlog.md` in that turn unless **close confirm** already appears in the thread.
- When this item depends on another item, do only the part that unblocks this item.
- When a blocker stops this item, tell the user what blocks it and wait.
- A new requirement becomes a new backlog item after the user confirms it. It is not added to the current item.
- Do not bundle two items into one implementation pass.

## Conflict handling

- When a user request conflicts with this rule (for example "finish the whole MVP at once" or "develop several features in parallel"), stop, tell the user the request conflicts with this rule, and confirm how to proceed.
- Offer two options: follow this rule item by item, or the user explicitly overrides this rule (record that confirmation). Until explicitly confirmed, default to this rule.
- Never silently comply with a conflicting request; never silently refuse it.

Wording checks: [friendly-language.mdc](./friendly-language.mdc).
